Speaker 1: And it is true that the NRC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.400
the National Republican Senatorial Committee, has&nbsp;
already decided to pull back a lot of their TV ad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.400
spending dollars because they're just giving up&nbsp;
on certain races. They don't think that there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.000
any point spending any money because it's&nbsp;
just going to be a waste. They might as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.320
consolidate that money and spend it in the places&nbsp;
where they do have an actual shot at winning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.920
And they've already spent a lot of their money&nbsp;
over the summer. Now they're having a tougher time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:41.440
fundraising because the political winds seem to&nbsp;
be going back in the Democratic direction. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.440
Republicans are in chaos right now. They thought&nbsp;
that they would have this big red wave, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.240
midterms, and now it's not looking so great. We're&nbsp;
seeing people turn on one another. We're seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.440
the rats leaving the ship. And as someone who&nbsp;
is not on their side, I like to see it happening

